-- title:
--   Transport of complete coefficient DVRs reading the same constants
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, let $W_0$ and $W$ be discrete valuation rings which are domains and are adically complete for their maximal ideals, and let $S$ be a commutative ring equipped with an ideal $I$ for which $S$ is $I$-adically Hausdorff (the only element congruent to $0$ modulo $I^n$ for every $n$ is $0$). Fix $\varpi \in A$ generating the maximal ideal of $A$. Assume given ring homomorphisms $\sigma_0 : A \to W_0$ and $\sigma : A \to W$ such that the maximal ideal of $W_0$ is generated by $\sigma_0(\varpi)$ and that of $W$ by $\sigma(\varpi)$, and such that every $w \in W_0$ (resp. every $w \in W$) differs from some $\sigma_0(a)$ (resp. some $\sigma(a)$), $a \in A$, by an element of the maximal ideal. Assume further given ring homomorphisms $C_0 : W_0 \to S$ and $C : W \to S$ carrying the maximal ideal of $W_0$, respectively of $W$, into $I$, and agreeing on $A$ in the sense that $C_0(\sigma_0 a) = C(\sigma a)$ for all $a \in A$. The conclusion is the existence of a ring isomorphism $\beta_W : W_0 \xrightarrow{\sim} W$ with $C_0(w) = C(\beta_W(w))$ for all $w \in W_0$ and $\beta_W(\sigma_0 a) = \sigma(a)$ for all $a \in A$.
--
--   This is a uniqueness statement for complete coefficient rings in the style of Cohen's structure theory: two complete discrete valuation rings that are topologically generated over a common discrete valuation ring $A$ (same uniformiser, residue field exhausted by $A$) are identified by a unique-up-to-the-stated-compatibilities isomorphism, and the identification is compatible with two $I$-adically continuous readings of constants into a separated ring $S$. It is used in the construction of local charts on the Drinfeld curve, to transport chart data together with its constants between two charts of one completed supersingular stalk.
